    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **61 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `selfLink` field on the owner representation so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `selfLink = \"/api/owners/\" + <owner id>`.\n\nThe response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec and populated via a MapStruct mapper, matching how the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `customerCode`, etc.) work. Two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `selfLink` computed as `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null-guarded on id), following the existing expression-based pattern.\n\nThis flows through the existing `getOwner` handler (which already maps the owner via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`), and also naturally appears on the create response for consistency. The targeted `Cp49Tests` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
